# Copy to .env (or .env.local) before running or building:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Both variables are read at build time and baked into the bundle. A production build
# refuses to run without VITE_API_MODE rather than quietly falling back to fixtures.
# Every VITE_ variable the browser bundle reads is listed here, and CI fails if that
# stops being true; see the deployment section of the README. The check compares this
# file against the import.meta.env reads in src/, which is exactly what ends up in the
# bundle.
#
# One VITE_ variable is deliberately not declared below, because it never reaches the
# bundle: VITE_PROXY_TARGET, read from process.env by vite.config.ts, points the dev
# server's /api proxy somewhere other than http://localhost:8008. It affects `npm run
# dev` only and has no effect on a build or a deployment.

# mock = offline fixtures, no backend and no routing traffic at all. This is the demo
#        build: it works on any static host, costs nothing, and shows a "mock" badge.
# live = real routing from the fiets-of-ov backend, at VITE_API_BASE below.
VITE_API_MODE=mock

# Where the backend is, in live mode. Ignored in mock mode. Two values are accepted:
#
#   /api                      the host proxies it on the same origin - the Vite dev
#                             server in development, functions/api/[[path]].js on
#                             Cloudflare Pages. No CORS, backend URL not in the bundle.
#   https://api.example.org   the browser calls the backend directly. The backend then
#                             has to serve HTTPS and allow the site's origin via CORS.
#
# Anything else fails the build, because nothing would serve it.
VITE_API_BASE=/api
